course: dictionary
lesson: 778
title: Beautifully, more than pretty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Beautifully is an adverb, a word that tells us how something is done. Its first meaning is in a beautiful way, so pleasant to see or hear. «The beds are clean and smell beautifully of lavender.» Here the smell is lovely and pleasant, so beautifully describes how the beds smell.
explain: Beautifully often means something is done very well, with great skill. When your teacher writes «You've written that beautifully», she is not talking about pretty handwriting. She means your work was done with care and skill. «She played beautifully» means she played very well.
explain: Beautifully can also mean perfectly or completely. «It worked beautifully» means it worked perfectly, with no problems. To check the meaning, put your idea into the sentence in place of the word and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Beautifully is an adverb, and it tells us how something is done.
fact: «Beautifully» can mean in a very pleasant way, as in «smell beautifully of lavender».
fact: «Beautifully» can mean very well or with great skill, as in «She played beautifully».
fact: «Beautifully» can mean perfectly or completely, as in «It worked beautifully».
fact: Good context check: if a sentence praises work, «beautifully» usually means done with great skill.
exercise: «She played beautifully.» What does beautifully mean here? | Very quietly | *Very well, with great skill | Only just | Slowly and with difficulty
exercise: Your teacher writes, «You've written that beautifully.» What is she praising? | How fast you wrote | The colour of your pencil | *Your work, done with great care and skill | Your handwriting is ugly
exercise: «The bird sang beautifully in the tree.» What does beautifully tell us? | How big the bird was | The time of day | The colour of the tree | *How the bird sang
test: «It worked beautifully.» What does beautifully mean? | Very loudly | Only a little | *Perfectly, completely | Slowly and with difficulty
test: «The beds are clean and smell beautifully of lavender.» What does beautifully tell us about the smell? | *Very pleasant | Very old | Very strong and burning | Like a petrol station
exam: Jayden says beautifully only means pretty to look at. Is he right? | No, it means very loudly | Yes, it only means something looks pretty | *No, it can also mean very well or perfectly | Yes, it always means happy
